# Orrery — Controls

This file defines how a player operates the game: the pointer that places and
drags on the field, the keyboard actions everything else runs on, and the
focus rule that routes the editing keys. What each verb does in the editor is
in `specs/editor.md`, and the menus and screens the navigation actions drive
are in `specs/ui.md`. Every figure below carries the name this specification
gives it.

## The pointer

{{#if (eq engine.slug "none")}}
This game stands on no engine, so the pointer belongs to the runtime layer you
write. What the game reads from that layer is a pointer position in the game's
logical units on the `STAGE_W x STAGE_H` (`1280 x 720`) stage, a press edge,
and a release edge. How the layer produces those three is yours to decide.
{{else if (eq engine.slug "simple-2d")}}
The pointer belongs to the engine, which documents it in the `engine/`
directory at the root of this repository. What the game reads from it is a
pointer position in the game's logical units on the `STAGE_W x STAGE_H`
(`1280 x 720`) stage, a press edge, and a release edge.
{{else}}
The pointer belongs to the engine, which documents it in the `engine/`
directory at the root of this repository. What the game reads from it is a
pointer position in the game's logical units on the `STAGE_W x STAGE_H`
(`1280 x 720`) stage, a press edge, and a release edge, delivered as the
ordered samples the player controller the game mode adds reads from the engine
each frame, so a drag that crossed several hexes between two frames arrives as
every position it visited rather than as the last one alone.
{{/if}}

The game acts on those three alone. Each pointer position is resolved on its
own, in the order the positions arrive, so a drag's ghost and a track being
laid follow the pointer hex by hex. What a press, a move, and a release do in
each region of the editor is defined in `specs/editor.md`; hexes are targeted
by the rule in `specs/field.md`, and tray slots and tape cells by the
rectangles `specs/editor.md` fixes. The pointer operates the editor alone.

`state.pointer` mirrors the pointer's position and press state every frame, as
`specs/state.md` describes.

## Focus

`state.editor.focus` is `field` or `tape`, and it routes the editing keys. A
press inside the tape panel's extent, `x >= TRAY_REGION_W` (`224`) and
`y >= TAPE_Y0` (`560`) as `specs/editor.md` fixes them, sets focus to `tape`;
a press anywhere else on the editor screen sets it to `field`. Focus is
`field` on entering the editor.

Two focus-routed actions share a physical key: `part-grow` and `ins-extend` on
`KeyW`, and `part-shrink` and `ins-retract` on `KeyS`. Each is registered on
its own, and the game reads the ones the current focus names.

## Actions and bindings

`ACTIONS` holds every action the game registers, and `BINDINGS` maps each to
the `KeyboardEvent.code` values that fire it. Each action is read as a press
edge, once per press, on the screens the table under What each screen reads
names.

### Navigation

| Action | Keys | Effect |
| --- | --- | --- |
| `up` | `ArrowUp` | Menus and select lists: moves the highlight up. Tape focus: moves the tape cursor to the previous row, as `specs/editor.md` states. |
| `down` | `ArrowDown` | Menus and select lists: moves the highlight down. Tape focus: moves the tape cursor to the next row, as `specs/editor.md` states. |
| `left` | `ArrowLeft` | How-to: previous page. Tape focus: moves the cursor one cell left, as `specs/editor.md` states. |
| `right` | `ArrowRight` | How-to: next page. Tape focus: moves the cursor one cell right, as `specs/editor.md` states. |
| `confirm` | `Enter` | Accepts the highlighted item. |
| `back` | `Escape` | Leaves the current screen; during a run, stops it, as `specs/simulation.md` states. |

### Global

| Action | Keys | Effect |
| --- | --- | --- |
| `mute` | `KeyM` | Toggles sound, from any screen. |
| `play` | `Space` | Editor: starts the run, or toggles running and paused. |
| `step` | `KeyN` | Editor: steps the run one cycle, as `specs/editor.md` states. |
| `speed-down` | `Comma` | Editor, during a run: the previous step of `SPEEDS`, as `specs/simulation.md` states. |
| `speed-up` | `Period` | Editor, during a run: the next step of `SPEEDS`, as `specs/simulation.md` states. |
| `undo` | `KeyU` | Editor, while editing: reverts the latest edit, as `specs/editor.md` defines. |
| `redo` | `KeyI` | Editor, while editing: re-applies the latest undone edit. |

### Field focus

| Action | Keys | Effect |
| --- | --- | --- |
| `part-cw` | `KeyE` | Rotates the selected or dragged part one step clockwise. |
| `part-ccw` | `KeyQ` | The same, counterclockwise. |
| `part-grow` | `KeyW` | Lengthens the selected or dragged arm within the bounds `specs/parts.md` fixes. |
| `part-shrink` | `KeyS` | Shortens the selected or dragged arm within the same bounds. |
| `part-delete` | `KeyX` | Removes the selected part. |

### Tape focus

| Action | Keys | Writes at the cursor |
| --- | --- | --- |
| `ins-rotate-ccw` | `KeyA` | `rotate-ccw` |
| `ins-rotate-cw` | `KeyD` | `rotate-cw` |
| `ins-extend` | `KeyW` | `extend` |
| `ins-retract` | `KeyS` | `retract` |
| `ins-pivot-ccw` | `KeyZ` | `pivot-ccw` |
| `ins-pivot-cw` | `KeyC` | `pivot-cw` |
| `ins-grab` | `KeyG` | `grab` |
| `ins-drop` | `KeyV` | `drop` |
| `ins-advance` | `KeyT` | `advance` |
| `ins-recede` | `KeyB` | `recede` |
| `ins-blank` | `Delete` | A blank. |
| `ins-erase` | `Backspace` | Nothing. It blanks the cell before the cursor, as `specs/editor.md` states. |
| `ins-reset` | `KeyR` | The `reset` macro of `specs/instructions.md`. |
| `ins-repeat` | `KeyY` | The `repeat` macro of `specs/instructions.md`. |

How writing at the cursor advances it, and how the tape panel scrolls to keep
the cursor visible, are in `specs/editor.md`.

## What each screen reads

| Screen | Live |
| --- | --- |
| `title` | `up` and `down` move the highlight; `confirm` takes it; `mute`. |
| `howto` | `left` and `right` turn the page; `confirm` and `back` return to `title`; `mute`. |
| `select` | `up` and `down` move the highlight; `confirm` opens the highlighted challenge when the mode's progression allows; `back` returns to `title`; `mute`. |
| `editor`, while editing | The pointer; the field-focus actions under `field` focus; the tape-focus actions and `up`, `down`, `left`, and `right` under `tape` focus; `undo`; `redo`; `play`; `step`; `back`; `mute`. |
| `editor`, `running` or `paused` | `play`, `step`, `speed-up`, `speed-down`, `back`, `mute`. |
| `editor`, `faulted` or `complete` | `back` and `mute`, and `up`, `down`, and `confirm` while the solved panel of `specs/ui.md` is up. |

An action a row omits does nothing on that screen.

## Out of scope

- Gamepad input. The editor is driven by the pointer and the keyboard.
- Rebinding. The bindings are fixed and the game offers no way to change
  them.
